[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m = (324\cos\theta - 504\sin\theta) + i(300\sin\theta + 504\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m = (324\cos\theta - 504\sin\theta) + i(276\sin\theta + 504\cos\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m The real part of the expression is \(324\cos\theta - 504\sin\theta\). To maximize this, we can use the method of Lagrange multipliers or recognize that the maximum value of \(a\cos\theta - b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = 504\), so the maximum value is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + 504^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 254016} = \sqrt{359092} = 599.2433
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m However, we need to check if this value can be achieved with the constraint \(|z| = 4\). The maximum value of the real part is indeed achieved when \(\cos\theta = \frac{324}{\sqrt{324^2 + 504^2}}\) and \(\sin\theta = \frac{-504}{\sqrt{324^2 + 504^2}}\). Let's calculate this explicitly:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m \cos\theta = \frac{324}{\sqrt{324^2 + 504^2}} = \frac{324}{599.2433} \approx 0.5407
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2357500)[0m \[
